  'rules.title': 'House rules', 'rules.edit': 'Edit text', 'rules.custom': 'Custom rules', 'rules.resetDefault': 'Restore original text',
  'rules.basic': 'The basic rule', 'rules.basicText': 'Every week (Monday to Sunday) the app assigns Floor, Bathroom and Kitchen. Base rule: you clean whatever you haven\'t cleaned in the longest, or whatever you owe. Assignment order: 1. Floor, 2. Bathroom, 3. Kitchen, 4. Rest.',
  'rules.home': 'How many are home',
  'rules.home4': '4 people: one chore each, the last one left rests.', 'rules.home3': '3 people: one chore each, nobody rests.',
  'rules.home2': '2 people: whoever hasn\'t done the Floor in the longest does it; the other does Bathroom and Kitchen. If whoever does the Floor also owes a make-up, they do two chores (Floor + make-up) and the other person only does what\'s left.',
  'rules.home1': '1 person: cleans everything.',
  'rules.makeups': 'Make-ups', 'rules.makeupsText': 'If one of your chores doesn\'t get done by you (skipped, or someone else does it for you), you owe a make-up on that chore. The app assigns it the first week you\'re home again, ON TOP of your normal turn that week. The make-up clears itself once you mark it "Done".',
  'rules.rests': 'Rests', 'rules.restsText': 'Cleaning for someone else earns a Rest credit. The app spends it as soon as it can: at least {n} people home and no open make-up. That week, you rest.',
  'rules.payback': 'Direct payback', 'rules.paybackText': 'Whoever covers for someone gets paid back directly, the first week both of them are home. The person who was covered for does the chore instead that week, and the one who covered gets it off completely. If the person paying back also owes a make-up of their own, that stays theirs — only their normal turn gets covered. It doesn\'t expire and is separate from the Rest credit.',
  'rules.absences': 'Absences and presence', 'rules.threeNights': 'THE 3-NIGHT RULE: if you sleep at home {n} or more nights (Monday to Sunday) you\'re in that week\'s cleaning.',
  'rules.markAway': 'If you sleep at home fewer than {n} nights, mark yourself away BY FRIDAY.', 'rules.noMark': 'If you don\'t mark yourself away by Friday, the app assigns you the chore. Skip it and it becomes a make-up (and a CDM).',
  'rules.results': 'How to log a result', 'rules.resDone': 'Done → the assigned person cleaned.', 'rules.resSkipped': 'Skipped → nobody cleaned: make-up for the assigned person, plus the CDM badge.',
  'rules.resBy': 'A name → that person cleaned instead of the assigned one: the assigned person still owes the make-up, and whoever cleaned earns a Rest credit.',
  'rules.resSkippedBy': '«Skipped (Name)» → Name was down to cover but also didn\'t clean: the make-up and the CDM go to Name instead, and the assigned person still owes their own.',
  'rules.resBlank': 'Blank → after Sunday (plus the grace days) it counts as Skipped. You can fix it any time: the app recalculates everything.',
  'rules.swaps': 'Agreed swaps', 'rules.swapsText': 'If two people agree to swap a chore without anyone skipping it, use "Swap chore": no make-up and no CDM, the chore counts as done.',
  'rules.badges': 'Badges', 'rules.trText': 'TR – Top Roommate: whoever cleaned the most within the ranking window (last {n} weeks).', 'rules.cdmText': 'CDM – earned by skipping a chore. Same window as the ranking.',
  'rules.badgesNote': 'Only finished weeks count. Covering for someone counts as cleaning, not as skipping.',
  'rules.moving': 'Moving in, moving out', 'rules.movingText': 'Moving out: put a leaving date. Moving in: the same slot as whoever left and a start date. The newcomer starts from zero, no inherited debt, with an adjustable starting priority.',
  'rules.daily': 'Daily house rules', 'rules.daily1': 'Weekly turns don\'t cancel daily responsibility: everyone washes their own dishes/pans, wipes the stove after cooking, and doesn\'t leave personal items around common areas.',
  'rules.daily2': 'The sink shouldn\'t stay piled with dirty dishes and/or pans for longer than strictly necessary.', 'rules.daily3': 'Trash: if the bin won\'t close, change the bag.',
  'rules.daily4': 'Bathroom: after a shower, open the window and raise the blind so the air can circulate and the bathroom doesn\'t go mouldy.',
  'rules.daily5': 'Running low on something: flag it in the Supplies list as soon as you notice. Or, if you know you\'ll rebuy it soon anyway, just rebuy it and log the expense on Tricount.',
  'rules.quality': 'Quality and deadlines', 'rules.q1': 'Cleaning has to be done properly and completely.', 'rules.q2': 'A sloppy clean counts as a chore NOT done.', 'rules.q3': 'Turns should be finished by Sunday whenever possible.',
  'rules.lastoutRule': 'Trips & holidays (last one out)', 'rules.lastoutText': 'This rule is independent of the weekly turns. Over holidays, or whenever everyone is away for an extended period, the last person to leave the house is responsible for the final check. Whoever leaves first still has to: take out their own trash, remove or eat their own perishables from the fridge and freezer, flag anything close to its expiry date for the others, and leave any common areas they used tidy.',
  'lastout.title': 'Last one out', 'lastout.hint': 'Tick everything before closing the door. The others see who did the check.', 'lastout.reset': 'New check', 'lastout.completed': 'Check completed by {name}',
  'lastout.progress': '{a} of {b}', 'lastout.allDone': 'All set: have a good trip! ✈️', 'lastout.edit': 'Edit list', 'lastout.addItem': 'Add item', 'lastout.lastBy': 'Last check: {name}, {when}',
  'lastout.i1': 'No perishable food left in the fridge or around the house', 'lastout.i2': 'The trash has been fully taken out', 'lastout.i3': 'AC units, heaters and any unnecessary appliances are switched off',
  'lastout.i4': 'Windows, doors, balconies and ALL taps (including the toilet\'s water valve) are shut', 'lastout.i5': 'Nothing is left running (water, gas, electricity)',
  'lastout.i6': 'I told the others about anything close to its expiry date', 'lastout.i7': 'The common areas I used are tidy',
